      "abstained": false,
      "answer": "Healthcare personnel transporting patients who are on Airborne Precautions do not need to wear a mask or respirator during transport if the patient is wearing a mask and infectious skin lesions are covered. If transport or movement outside an AIIR is necessary, instruct patients to wear a surgical mask, if possible.",
