      "abstained": false,
      "answer": "Infections transmitted via the airborne route, such as M tuberculosis, measles and chickenpox, require additional precautions, and suspected patients should be placed in an examination room, preferably an AIIR, as soon as possible. Airborne Precautions also cover tuberculosis and possibly SARS-CoV, and the preferred placement for patients who require Airborne Precautions is in an airborne infection isolation room (AIIR).",
