      "abstained": false,
      "answer": "Vaccines should be placed in a freezer at a temperature range between -50°C and -15°C (-58°F and +5°F), or between -90°C and -60°C (-130°F and -76°F) for ultra-cold freezer storage. The range is between -90°C and -60°C (-130°F and -76°F) for an ultra-cold freezer. Never leave vaccines in a storage unit that does not maintain temperatures within the recommended range.",
