      "abstained": false,
      "answer": "Never store food and beverages in the unit with vaccines, and avoid placing or storing any items other than vaccines, diluents, and water bottles inside storage units. Frequent opening of the refrigerator door to retrieve food items can adversely affect the internal temperature of the unit and potentially damage the vaccines. Also, never store vaccines in the freezer compartment of household-grade combination refrigerator/freezer units because they have cold spots and temperature fluctuations.",
